From: Mika Ala-Sippola <mika.ala-sippola@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: restore rxstate in musb_ep_restart to fix RX packet drop

Commit 3fc137386c46 ("usb: musb: Fix hardware lockup on first Rx endpoint
request") replaced the call to rxstate(musb, req) in musb_ep_restart()
with MUSB_RXCSR_FLUSHFIFO.

While intended to avoid synchronously calling req->complete from within
usb_ep_queue() for u_ether, flushing the RX FIFO whenever a request is
queued discards any valid packet that arrived while no request was
enqueued in userspace gadgets (e.g. FunctionFS / ADB, mass storage,
USB serial).

In protocols like ADB, the host sends the 24-byte header followed
immediately by the payload. Once adbd reads the header and issues a read
for the payload, musb_ep_restart() flushes the FIFO, permanently discarding
the already-ACKed payload and hanging the connection forever.

Restore the call to rxstate() when starting an RX request so pending
FIFO data is unloaded into the enqueued request buffer.

Signed-off-by: Mika Ala-Sippola <mika.ala-sippola@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c | 11 ++---------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
index c6076df0d50c..910f50967627 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
@@ -1163,15 +1163,8 @@ void musb_ep_restart(struct musb *musb, struct musb_request *req)
 {
-	u16 csr;
-	void __iomem *epio = req->ep->hw_ep->regs;
-
 	trace_musb_req_start(req);
 	musb_ep_select(musb->mregs, req->epnum);
-	if (req->tx) {
+	if (req->tx)
 		txstate(musb, req);
-	} else {
-		csr = musb_readw(epio, MUSB_RXCSR);
-		csr |= MUSB_RXCSR_FLUSHFIFO | MUSB_RXCSR_P_WZC_BITS;
-		musb_writew(epio, MUSB_RXCSR, csr);
-		musb_writew(epio, MUSB_RXCSR, csr);
-	}
+	else
+		rxstate(musb, req);
 }
